  "id": "implicit-association-test",
  "term": "Implicit Association Test",
  "definition": "The Implicit Association Test is a sorting task used in research to measure how strongly people automatically link target categories with attribute categories, such as flowers versus insects and pleasant versus unpleasant. It is widely used in social cognition and other fields to study automatic associations.",
